2025-09-30 20:59:05,714 [WARNING] Skipped idx=179: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='Supporting sentence: In humans, three TAp73 isoforms (TAp73α, TAp73β, and TAp73γ) have been identified. These isoforms are produced through alternative splicing of the p73 gene and are characterized by their ability to transactivate target genes that promote apoptosis and cell cycle arrest, contributing to the chemosensitivity observed in BRCA1-deficient ovarian carcinoma cells.'
2025-09-30 20:59:05,714 [WARNING] Skipped idx=180: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='Supporting sentence: In humans, two TAp73 isoforms have been identified: TAp73α and TAp73β. These isoforms are produced by alternative splicing of the TP73 gene and differ in their N-terminus. TAp73α is the longer isoform with a molecular weight of approximately 56 kDa, while TAp73β is the shorter isoform with a molecular weight of about 48 kDa. Both isoforms can form homodimers or heterodimers with other p53 family members, including p53, and can translocate to the nucleus in response to various stress signals. They play roles in cell cycle regulation, apoptosis, and DNA damage response.'
